_{0}.$\n\nIn plain words, this means that solutions that start sufficiently close to the equilibrium remain close, but may not converge to the equilibrium.\n\n- An equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}$ is called *asymptotically stable* if it is stable and there exists a neighborhood $O$ of ${x}^{∗}$ such that every orbit that begins inside $O$ approaches ${x}^{∗}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nIn plain words, this means that solutions that start sufficiently close to the equilibrium remain close and converge to the equilibrium as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- An equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}$ is called *unstable* if it is not stable.\n\nIn plain words, this means that solutions eventually move away from the equilibrium for some initial conditions arbitrarily close to it.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"Stable but not asymptotically stable.\"" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359474 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359475 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359476 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359477 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359478 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1041 "selection" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359477 13194139535657 true] [17592186359473 1110 #uuid "9ac1cde9-39f2-5443-a24a-e79a254128b0" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359474 1034 "Asymptotically stable only for certain initial conditions." 13194139535657 true] [17592186359474 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535657 true] [17592186359474 1111 #uuid "db6c711e-a164-50b5-bfec-66eb3cd983c3" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359475 1034 "Unstable." 13194139535657 true] [17592186359475 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535657 true] [17592186359475 1111 #uuid "d7ffea3e-b54a-599a-a784-6d10da09dad4" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359476 1034 "Asymptotically stable." 13194139535657 true] [1759218635