aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={y}^{2}(t)-x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of differential equations above?" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359486 1113 #uuid "a345a07a-9a32-5621-bbdf-168369d7d55d" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359486 1145 "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y=0\\,⇒\\,y=2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $y$ into the second equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-x & =0 \\\\ (2x)^{2}-x & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x & =0 \\\\ x(4x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\text{ }\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $y:$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y=2\\cdot 0=0.$\n\n- For $x=\\frac{1}{4},$ we get $y=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359488 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359489 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359490 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359491 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359492 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1041 "selection" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359491 13194139535657 true] [17592186359487 1110 #uuid "fb26ac33-1571-50cd-aa57-eb7e5c01f475" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359488 1034 "$[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]$ only" 13194139535657 true] [17592186359488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535657 true] [17592186359488 1111 #uuid "0e78d487-79b6-5de2-b365-